  "facts": [
    "Fort McHenry Tunnel, opened November 23, 1985, was built using 32 prefabricated steel tubes, each 82 feet wide and 42 feet tall, sunk into the Patapsco River via the immersed tube method.",
    "The tunnel’s construction, led by K‑R‑T, cost $750 million in 1985 dollars—equivalent to $2.2 billion today—making it the most expensive Interstate project until Boston’s Big Dig surpassed it.",
    "After the Francis Scott Key Bridge collapsed March 26, 2024, Fort McHenry Tunnel became a primary alternate route for non‑hazardous trucks, underscoring its critical regional role."
